3. The face helper (a separate download the plugin fetches when you ask for it, not in the plugin zip)

  Face analysis uses Google's MediaPipe Face Landmarker model (Apache License 2.0) and the MediaPipe, NumPy, OpenCV, Matplotlib, Pillow and Python packages, downloaded by the user on request from python.org, PyPI and Google. Each keeps its own licence.

  The list the plugin downloads, with versions and hashes, is src/Soundstage/Face/face-pack.json. Licences as read from
  PyPI on 21/11/2026:
    Face Landmarker model (face_landmarker.task, float16/1)   Apache-2.0
    Pose Landmarker model (pose_landmarker_full, float16/1)   Apache-2.0 (Google's model card; src/Soundstage/Face/pose-pack.json)
    Python embeddable 3.14.5                                   PSF-2.0
    mediapipe 1.2.3, absl-py 2.5.1, flatbuffers 25.12.19       Apache-2.0
    opencv-python-headless 5.1.0.95                            Apache-2.0 (the wheel also bundles FFmpeg under LGPL-2.1, per the opencv-python project)
    numpy 2.5.5                                                BSD-3-Clause and others, per PyPI
    matplotlib 3.11.2                                          Matplotlib licence (PSF-based)
    pillow 13.0.0                                              MIT-CMU
    certifi, packaging, pyparsing, cycler, python-dateutil, kiwisolver, fonttools   each wheel's own licence
  Nothing from this list is redistributed by Soundstage. It is downloaded straight from the official sources, checked
  against a pinned SHA-256, and kept in the plugin's own config folder.

4. Plugins Soundstage talks to (not shipped, not changed)

  Stagehand, Brio, Glamourer and Penumbra are separate Dalamud plugins you install yourself. Soundstage only calls their
  public IPC.

5. AI providers (optional, your own key)

  Soundstage can send a picture to Google Gemini, OpenRouter or a server you name, using a key you paste in. Those are
  their services under their own terms. See SETUP-AI.md.
